affd51f2f1b8807e091af366d", "bytes": 170443, "lines": 419, "events_no_deltas": [{"type": "system", "subtype": "init", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "tools": ["StructuredOutput"], "mcp_servers": [], "permissionMode": "auto", "claude_code_version": "2.1.294", "output_style": "default", "init_sha256": "19a6ffcf0781096cd8fadcc901d1f698c81748761870f4f438dc6f07a56b3d9a"}, {"type": "system", "subtype": "status", "status": "requesting"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "message_start", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgB9HJSVi89oscnENiZeb", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3785, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3785}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "ttft_ms": 1348, "thinking_display": "updates"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 0, "content_block": {"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "thinking_display": "updates"}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgB9HJSVi89oscnENiZeb", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": {"длина": 28612, "sha256": "dd4e3564c056425674ad560cd1a321ffb2c17d28e84ea5c5c080e38ae316c4aa"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3785, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3785}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T06:46:13.844Z", "request_id": "req_011CgB9HJ1wjrsaiX1MqXr1L", "thinking_duration_ms": 107444}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 0}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 1, "content_block": {"type": "text", "text": ""}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgB9HJSVi89oscnENiZeb", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I pick **candidate 4**, the plan that orders exactly the forecast, though this rests on rough mental estimates rather than a precise simulation. Each daily order matches the forecast for its arrival day (order on day t = mu[t+L]), and it beats the other plans because it piles up the least surplus stock.\n\n**What every plan loses at the start.** No plan can avoid the opening shortfall. The first product 1 delivery arrives on day 4, so 54 units of stock face about 138 units of demand (roughly 84 short). The first product 0 delivery arrives on day 2, so 24 units face about 41 (roughly 17 short). This penalty is the same for every candidate, so it doesn't change the ranking.\n\n**Why ordering more is a loss here.** The plan is fixed in advance and doesn't react to what actually sells. Stock behaves like a running total of (order − demand) that can't drop below zero.\n- If you order more than average demand, the surplus grows every day. You pay storage on it every day until the end, and whatever is left at the end was bought for nothing.\n- Spoilage only starts once stock gets close to 4–6 days' worth, so it doesn't cap the build-up early on.\n- An extra unit only pays off if it heads off a shortage within the next few days. That gets less likely as the backlog of stock grows.\n\n**Rough cost of the overstock for product 1.** Average demand is about 1.046 × forecast, with a spread of about 14 units a day. Over the 26 days, against a plan ordering exactly average demand:\n\n| Order size vs. forecast | Daily surplus | Purchases + penalties + storage (relative) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1.00 (candidate 4) | about −2 | about 1600 |\n| 1.05 (candidate 7) | about 0 | about 1760 |\n| 1.10 (candidates 0 and 2) | about +2.4 | about 2190 |\n| 1.15 (candidate 3) | about +4.6 | about 2870 |\n| 1.19 (candidate 6) | about +6.3 | about 3530, plus spoilage and a full warehouse |\n\nProduct 0 follows the same pattern on a smaller scale. Candidates 3 and 4 order exactly the forecast for it, and the others order more.\n\n**Plans that order less often (1 and 5).** Skipping days saves the 26 order fee, but whatever is ordered for later days sits in storage overnight.\n- Candidate 1 orders every other day. The extra storage is about 52 per two-day cycle, against 26 saved. On top of that it orders about 1.1 × forecast, so it is worse than candidate 0.\n- Candidate 5 orders every three days. The extra storage is about 157 per cycle against 52 saved, and deliveries of up to about 200 units overflow the 208-unit warehouse. It is clearly worse.\n\n**Uncertainty.** Candidate 4 runs short somewhat more often. But with this cost structure, a shortage costs less than carrying surplus stock until the end, so its downside is smaller. The order 4 > 7 > 0 ≈ 2 > 3 > 6 holds up unless demand runs well above forecast for most of the month."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3785, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3785}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_t